afk: brainstorming blocks its todo phase for the duration of the dialogue.

Motivation: the harness sends a stop-time reminder whenever an assistant
turn ends with pending/in_progress todos (omp
packages/coding-agent/src/session/todo-tracker.ts, checkCompletion), plus
a mid-run nudge after 12 mutating tool calls (takeMidRunNudge). This
skill mandates a task per checklist item AND one question per message,
so every brainstorming turn trips it: the agent gets nudged toward
execution in the middle of a design conversation.

`blocked` is the existing, documented state for "open but waiting on
external input", and both reminder paths filter to pending/in_progress
only, so blocking the phase suppresses them without disabling reminders
globally or touching omp. A forgotten unblock cannot strand the list:
writing-plans opens with a fresh `todo init`, which replaces the phases
outright.

What must survive a rebase:
- The block instruction sits with the checklist preamble, so it runs
  before the first turn that can end with open todos.
- Checklist item 9 (transition to implementation) unblocks before
  handing off to writing-plans.

